7.Reflection questions:
1. Why is Gaussian preferred over a large box low-pass filter?
A Gaussian filter produces smoother frequency responses and reduces abrupt changes in the frequency domain.
It also creates more natural-looking blur with fewer unwanted artifacts.

2. What does separability do for computational cost?
A separable 2D Gaussian filter can be implemented using two 1D filtering operations(horizontal and vertical) which reduces computational complexity.

3. How do boundary modes change corners and edges?
Replicate: Repeats the nearest edge pixel.
Symmetric: Reflects the image at its boundary.
Circular: Wraps pixels from the opposite side.
These methods produce different results near image boundaries.
